    {
      "id": "p1",
      "text": "The grid system orchestrator initiated a system-wide power alert after a generating unit suffered a critical malfunction, an energy infrastructure failure that exposed the fragile balance of the island group's power grid. With nine hundred fifty megawatts of capacity loss, emergency measures were required to stabilize the system.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Creator",
        "fragments": [
          "why-0",
          "how-1",
          "result-0"
        ],
        "center": "how-1",
        "center_kind": "how",
        "channel": "toned",
        "channel_role": "element_centered",
        "composition_mode": "ADR-0008",
        "salience_rank": 0
      },
      "warnings": [],
      "fit": 0.85
    },
    {
      "id": "p2",
      "text": "Emergency response architects executed a precision load-reduction design to prevent a critical transmission line from overloading. This control action, a grid stabilization measure, was the direct response to an equipment failure at a power plant component, part of a series of extended facility shutdowns that created a massive power deficit.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Creator",
        "fragments": [
          "why-0",
          "why-1",
          "how-2",
          "result-0"
        ],
        "center": "how-2",
        "center_kind": "how",
        "channel": "toned",
        "channel_role": "element_centered",
        "composition_mode": "ADR-0008",
        "salience_rank": 1
      },
      "warnings": [],
      "fit": 0.82
    },
    {
      "id": "p3",
      "text": "The energy sector entity, facing a grid incident and prolonged plant failures, was forced to manage a colossal generation void. The seasonal heat drove demand into a thin operating margin, creating an energy demand spike that strained the entire organization's capacity to maintain supply.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Creator",
